  "id": "COMPOUND:32001 - PROTEIN:5943",
  "verbalization": "Koaburaside is implicated in the regulation of Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP through a series of target relationships, with the latter being a common endpoint across multiple pathways. The evidence suggests that Koaburaside acts as a target of multiple compounds, including Antrocinnamomins A, (2S)-2,4-dimethylpentanal, and 3',5-Dihydroxy-4',6,7,8-Tetramethoxyflavone, all of which are known to target the same set of proteins, namely EZH2/SUZ12/EED/RBBP7/RBBP4. This indicates a potential mechanism where Koaburaside may influence the activity of these enzymes through the compounds it interacts with, ultimately affecting the function of Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP. The shared target profile suggests a possible functional link between Koaburaside and the phosphatase, possibly through a common pathway or a direct interaction. The evidence supports a role for Koaburaside in modulating the activity of this phosphatase, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
